Use Arg request, response
response~content_type = "text/plain"
-- Probe for the PUT/DELETE body/argument contract (v99, Diseño 2). Reports the
-- method, the parsed argument count and pairs (which for GET/PUT/DELETE come
-- from the query string and for POST from the body), and the raw body left
-- untouched in ~post_string. Lets a test prove that a PUT/DELETE takes its args
-- from the query while its body stays raw and available -- and that stdin was
-- drained (no hang).
Say "method="request~method
n = request~arg()
Say "argcount="n
Do i = 1 To n
  Say i": "request~arg(i,"Name")"="request~arg(i,"Value")
End
Say "body=["request~post_string"]"
